WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.560
Even before she was a fully-fledged doctor, Kate&nbsp;
Barker always had a fascination for the outdoors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.600
Growing up, being out among nature felt like&nbsp;
she was connected to the wider world, one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.520
part of a larger whole. She intuited from a very&nbsp;
young age that the Earth had a system in place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.720
full of millions if not billions of parts that&nbsp;
all worked together in the hopes of achieving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:29.040
perfect balance. Humans, animals, and insects,&nbsp;
right the way down to germs that were so small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:35.440
they couldn’t be seen unless under a microscope.
And then, of course, there were the plants; trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.080
flowers, and all manner of other flora that&nbsp;
provided the world with so much more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.600
making it look beautiful. And it was, so much&nbsp;
so that a young Kate wanted to devote her life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.360
to helping maintain our beautiful little blue and&nbsp;
green planet, and understanding every part of it.&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.240
The ways she did that changed as the years went&nbsp;
on. As a child, it was learning how trees take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:02.080
in carbon dioxide and water, then use the sun’s&nbsp;
energy to feed themselves and produce oxygen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.720
through a process known as photosynthesis.&nbsp;
Then, in high school, Kate was writing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.720
giving presentations on the importance of&nbsp;
protecting the environment and conserving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.840
wildlife, trying to convince her classmates&nbsp;
to see the world in the same way she did.&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.040
By the time college rolled around, that protection&nbsp;
took on a seemingly more proactive form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.960
standing out on picket lines in protest when&nbsp;
the college announced it would be chopping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.800
down its nearby woods to expand the campus.
Eventually, she was made Doctor Kate Barker, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:37.360
awarded her PhD in Botany and Plant Science. She&nbsp;
thought that would be when the real work began;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.440
having climbed her way up to achieving&nbsp;
her degree was only the first step,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:46.240
the next would involve working tirelessly to&nbsp;
keep the world’s greenery alive. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.760
Kate had studied for years, learning about&nbsp;
anything and everything to do with plant life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:57.120
their different functions and structures, how&nbsp;
each species had evolved and could be classified,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.640
and how they all formed part&nbsp;
of the planet’s ecosystem.&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:06.560
Unfortunately, even for those with the noblest of&nbsp;
intentions, the harsh, unforgiving laws of reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.400
can tend to get in the way. In Kate’s case, that&nbsp;
came in the form of being snapped up for a job at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.760
a genetic research company. Sure, on the one hand&nbsp;
she did get to rely on all the information she had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.840
learned on her way to earning her PhD. But, on the&nbsp;
downside, all Kate got to use her knowledge for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.640
was receiving and tending to various plant&nbsp;
samples. Getting asked occasionally to run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.880
tests on those samples was about the&nbsp;
pinnacle of excitement in her job.&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.440
Somehow, despite working with plants, Doctor&nbsp;
Barker couldn’t help but feel further away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.880
nature than she had ever been. That was until an&nbsp;
unusual specimen was brought to her department for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:48.880
analysis, something unlike anything Kate had&nbsp;
seen in all her years of research and study.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.360
Although she didn’t know it at the time,&nbsp;
this unique plant would bring Doctor Barker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:03:01.280
closer to nature in a way she could never have&nbsp;
imagined… because it was a sample of SCP-306.&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.920
Of course, at the time, and even after the&nbsp;
plant’s anomalous properties began to take effect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.040
Kate was completely unaware of this. When it was&nbsp;
first brought to her lab, it seemed like just an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.440
ordinary fungus. No one had been able&nbsp;
to successfully identify it, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.160
but if anyone could, Doctor Kate Barker&nbsp;
was perhaps the best-qualified person.&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.920
“Where was it found?” she asked the lab&nbsp;
technician as he handed her the sample,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.840
secured in a sealed, airtight container.
“Pretty close to here apparently,” the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.240
lab tech replied. “Louisiana swamps are always&nbsp;
full of mushrooms and stuff like this, right?”&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.560
“Yes, that’s true. There are quite a few&nbsp;
different fungi native to Louisiana.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.280
Kate answered instinctively, like her brain was&nbsp;
on autopilot; she was more focused on examining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.960
the sample in the box than the conversation.
“Thing is, no one knows what kind this is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.280
or if it’s dangerous. I heard a rumor the&nbsp;
locals used to call it ‘Frog Rot’, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.280
apparently that was an older name for it,” the&nbsp;
technician added, garnering little more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.080
a mumble of agreement from the doctor of botany.
Kate placed the clear, Perspex container near the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.480
window, letting the natural light of the outdoors&nbsp;
give her a better look at what was inside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.000
It was a portion of a dead tree, its bark soggy&nbsp;
and darkened from the swamp water. Growing out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.000
of its side was a cluster of the mysterious fungus&nbsp;
in question, looking more like pustules or a cyst,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.360
a tumor growing out of the dead wood, as if it&nbsp;
had drained the bigger plant of all its life.&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.480
Kate’s next few hours were spent taking samples of&nbsp;
the fungus, keeping her hands and face covered as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:31.680
she scraped away part of it to examine under her&nbsp;
microscope. There was little abnormal about it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:37.360
on a cellular level, nothing in testing to suggest&nbsp;
that the sample was toxic or directly harmful. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:42.160
Kate could decipher about the plant was that it&nbsp;
was related to a certain genus of fungi known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:47.760
Trichophyton – which includes the same parasitic&nbsp;
varieties of fungus that can cause athlete's foot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.200
ringworm, and similar infections in humans.
Still unable to fully identify the species,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.240
Kate decided to take a closer&nbsp;
look at how it was growing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.560
Putting the container behind a safety screen,&nbsp;
she opened it up and began to pull apart the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:06.320
sodden tree bark with her gloved hands. There was&nbsp;
definitely some kind of mass underneath the bark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.960
what Kate initially assumed to be the wood of&nbsp;
the tree that the fungus had taken root to…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:16.400
nothing could have prepared her for how wrong she&nbsp;
was. As the bark split apart and crumbled away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.320
it revealed what was underneath&nbsp;
it: a cottontail swamp rabbit.&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.160
The fungi took on even more of a tumor-like&nbsp;
appearance when Doctor Barker saw that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.640
was actually growing out of the rabbit’s&nbsp;
back, having actually taken root within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.840
the poor creature’s body. As much as the sight&nbsp;
of it was profoundly upsetting – even a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:39.040
sickening – the scientist in Kate knew that this&nbsp;
was all just part of nature taking its course.&nbsp;

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:44.160
Once she got over the initial shock, it was even&nbsp;
a little fascinating. Her botanical expertise was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:49.440
second to none, and through that knowledge, she&nbsp;
knew that most fungi grew in damp conditions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.160
But she had never seen any genus grow from&nbsp;
the biological matter of another organism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.160 --> 00:06:01.040
dead nor alive. Could this mystery species&nbsp;
grow in any biomass? Even in a human being?&nbsp;

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:07.120
Worried about that possibility, Kate went to store&nbsp;
the SCP-306 sample until further testing could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:12.240
conducted. As she placed it back in the container,&nbsp;
her hand nudged one of the fungi’s bulbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.960
causing it to expel a wisp of tiny spores.&nbsp;
Not that she could see them of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.960
they were microscopically small.&nbsp;
But as they drifted through the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.760
the spores were drawn to Kate, up and up towards&nbsp;
where she was steadily breathing. The minute the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:31.040
spores slipped undetected into her airway, Doctor&nbsp;
Barker immediately began coughing, feeling a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:35.840
disgusting, earthy tang at the back of her throat.
She couldn’t stop spluttering, instinctively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.320
raising her hand to cover her mouth. Her rubber&nbsp;
gloves were still covering her fingers, coated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:46.240
in even more invisible residue from the fungus,&nbsp;
and now Kate was unknowingly breathing in more.&nbsp;

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.560
Excusing herself from work for the rest of&nbsp;
the day, Doctor Kate Barker went home feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:56.320
sicker and sicker as every minute passed. Her&nbsp;
fever was climbing rapidly, limbs shuddering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:00.720
and still, she couldn’t stop coughing and&nbsp;
spluttering as she tried to expel a foul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:06.720
lingering sensation that refused to leave her&nbsp;
throat. But those weren’t even the worst symptoms.&nbsp;

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.760
Two days had come and gone since the incident in&nbsp;
the lab, and Kate still hadn’t returned to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:17.840
job. How could she? She felt awful, and looked far&nbsp;
worse. Large lesions had started appearing on her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:22.960
skin, rapidly turning into warts. Just looking&nbsp;
at them made Kate’s stomach turn, and on a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:28.080
occasions, poking at them and feeling these alien&nbsp;
lumps on her skin caused her to vomit. Every night&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.960
she would go to bed, her body rapidly switching&nbsp;
from swelteringly hot, then becoming cold enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.880
to cause Kate to shiver uncontrollably.
At first, it looked like the lesions were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:41.840
clearing, falling away from her skin soon after&nbsp;
they had fully formed into warts. But the fleeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.880
bit of hope that gave her was quickly wiped away&nbsp;
when new ones started to grow in their place.&nbsp;

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.360
This didn’t just feel like flu, or any&nbsp;
other type of sickness for that matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:57.600
It felt painful, on the deepest, tiniest level.&nbsp;
During what little restless sleep she did get,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:02.000
Kate kept having nightmares about doctors&nbsp;
looking at her cells under a microscope,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.680
watching them changing into… something else.&nbsp;
It had been over two weeks since she had first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:14.400
been exposed to the SCP-306 spores, and still,&nbsp;
she hadn’t been well enough to go back to work.&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.800
Each time Kate had called the human resources&nbsp;
department to inform them she still wasn’t any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.920
better, they always came out with the same advice;&nbsp;
drink plenty of fluids, try to eat, and keep your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:29.040
strength up. Doctor Barker hadn’t stopped eating&nbsp;
or drinking, albeit at a very slightly reduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:33.440
rate. Her appetite had been sapped along&nbsp;
with most of her energy, although she had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.240
noticed that she’d dropped a significant amount&nbsp;
of weight in an alarmingly short amount of time.&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.640
Three weeks later, Kate flicked on the&nbsp;
bathroom light and barely recognized herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:48.000
Not only was she no longer at a healthy weight,&nbsp;
but her skin… something was very wrong with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.920
skin. She had developed an abnormal pigmentation,&nbsp;
a yellowish, greenish hue almost like she had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.920 --> 00:09:00.560
somehow developed jaundice. But to the touch, it&nbsp;
felt strange, almost a rubbery texture. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:04.960
if she hadn’t felt so sick, Kate would have&nbsp;
noticed that her skin wasn’t absorbing water the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:11.360
way it used to either, displaying the same type&nbsp;
of permeability as the skin of most amphibians.&nbsp;

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.240
Two months had gone past and nobody at the&nbsp;
research company had heard a word from Kate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.200
She wasn’t answering her phone, a few of them&nbsp;
were asked to go to her apartment to check on her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.240
but she never came to the door either. None&nbsp;
of them had any idea what had happened, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:32.000
certainly didn’t know the changes that her body&nbsp;
had undergone… and none of them painlessly either.&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.800
The constant pain Kate had been feeling had&nbsp;
gradually built and built, until it felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:42.480
parts of her body were twisting and contorting&nbsp;
against her will and in unnatural ways. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:47.440
the grinding feeling of her bones pulling each&nbsp;
other as they shrank, her limbs were wracked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:52.240
with unbearable agony. At the same time, her&nbsp;
stomach had shrunk to the point where she wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:57.920
even able to eat anymore. The same reduction&nbsp;
was occurring to the rest of her organs too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:04.160
heart, liver, lungs, brain, everything was getting&nbsp;
smaller, shrinking organs imprisoned within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:10.880
a skeleton that was also decreasing in size.
Then, one morning, the pain had seemingly stopped.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:15.200
After a night spent screaming in sheer&nbsp;
agony, tears streaming down her face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:20.400
Kate woke up on the floor of her apartment&nbsp;
under a pile of her clothes. But as she awoke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:26.000
she instantly noticed something. Everything looked&nbsp;
bigger, the whole room towered above her like she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:30.480
had been reduced down to the size of something&nbsp;
much smaller than a human. She tried opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:36.640
her mouth to say something, anything, but her lips&nbsp;
couldn’t form words anymore. Her arms felt strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:41.280
too, like their reach was somehow much shorter,&nbsp;
the same with her legs that were now tucked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:49.440
under her body. Her tiny, rubbery-skinned&nbsp;
body… SCP-306 had turned her into a frog.&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.840
It took Kate almost an entire day to&nbsp;
figure out how to properly move around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:58.720
first needing a long time to emotionally process&nbsp;
what had happened to her. If she had still been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.680
able to, she would have been sick and cried&nbsp;
endlessly, wailing on the floor. Instead, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:09.200
she tried to make any noise, a tiny croak was all&nbsp;
that emanated from the back of her hoarse throat.&nbsp;

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.280
But before she could find a way to leave&nbsp;
her apartment, someone else found their way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:18.400
in. From way down on the floor, the men in&nbsp;
their white hazard suits looked colossal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:23.600
impossibly tall. Kate tried her best to dodge&nbsp;
between the thick soles of their heavy boots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:28.080
as they came crashing down towards her from&nbsp;
above, each one having enough force behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:33.200
it to crush her in an instant. She leaped out of&nbsp;
the way of one descending boot, only to be caught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:38.960
mid-air in a glass container. As the lid screwed&nbsp;
tightly shut, sealing her inside, Kate was lifted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:43.200
up and saw a patch on the hazmat uniforms&nbsp;
of the men that had come to take her away:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.800
a black circle, with three arrows pointing in&nbsp;
towards its center, and an outline surrounding it.&nbsp;

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:54.000
The Foundation put her in a glass tank with eleven&nbsp;
other frogs, each of them looking almost identical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:58.880
to Kate, all climbing over each other, fighting&nbsp;
for their own space in the tiny enclosure. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:04.160
the moment she arrived, Kate could see the same&nbsp;
thing in their gaze as they could see in hers;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:10.480
sadness, unmistakable even in those dark, beady&nbsp;
little eyes. These were people, or at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:16.640
they had been human beings at some point. But now&nbsp;
anything on the outside that had made them unique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:22.160
their individuality, had been taken away, and&nbsp;
their minds had all been locked inside the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:27.280
frog-shaped body as Kate now found herself in.
Over the next few months, the Foundation had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:32.160
their scientists running a series of tests on&nbsp;
the frogs, who were now all categorized under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:39.120
the collective designation of SCP-306-1. Even&nbsp;
though she was unable to speak, Kate recognized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.160
their methodical scientific process, how they&nbsp;
would test one or two of the frogs at a time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.200
note the results, then change a variable and&nbsp;
repeat the test to see if there were any changes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:54.000
It was the same process she used to go through&nbsp;
every time a new sample arrived at her lab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.360
Watching the researchers reminded her of her old&nbsp;
job, the life she’d worked so hard for, and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:04.880
cruelly reminded that it was all gone now. Nobody&nbsp;
would ever know where she went. She’d never get to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:10.400
be out among nature the way she had always loved.
Kate had long since figured out the root cause of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:14.960
her transformation; a while after she had started&nbsp;
to feel sick, she’d wondered if that strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:20.080
fungus had anything to do with it. Seeing all the&nbsp;
Foundation scientists and guards in their hazmat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:25.600
gear, only handling the other frogs with thick&nbsp;
rubber gloves, seemed to prove her theory right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:31.200
and suggested that she and her fellow amphibians&nbsp;
were still infectious. Still, she currently had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:36.000
no way of communicating with the Foundation&nbsp;
personnel about what had caused her to change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:40.560
although they seemed as if they already knew.
Most of the tests involved the researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:46.560
putting Kate and the other frogs into mazes, or&nbsp;
making them solve puzzles, or memorizing commands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:51.840
Naturally, having once been human, they all picked&nbsp;
it up quicker than the researchers expected. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:56.400
their perspective, these frogs were displaying&nbsp;
an extremely advanced form of intelligence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:00.320
Gradually, the testing progressed and the&nbsp;
Foundation’s researchers began attempting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:05.280
teach the frog specimens to read and write,&nbsp;
all skills that they already possessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:10.240
even if some of them needed some time to learn&nbsp;
how to hold a pen in their new sticky fingers.&nbsp;

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:16.320
Kate herself was made to complete an IQ test,&nbsp;
scoring 127 points. Now that she had a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:22.480
communicate with these scientists through writing&nbsp;
notes, she and the other SCP-306-1s were asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:26.560
their names. That was the moment the&nbsp;
Foundation realized what they were.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:32.720
These weren’t just frogs, but human beings&nbsp;
who were now trapped in the bodies of frogs.&nbsp;

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:37.440
Perhaps inspired by this human-to-frog&nbsp;
transformation, or possibly as some cruel joke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:42.720
one of the Foundation’s researchers – who went by&nbsp;
the name Thomson – brought in a children’s book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:49.200
and presented it to the collection of SCP-306-1&nbsp;
specimens. At first, Kate enjoyed the simplicity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:54.560
of the stories, and it seemed her fellow frogs did&nbsp;
as well. But gradually they all grew depressed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.560 --> 00:15:00.000
Maybe one of the stories featured a prince&nbsp;
being turned from a frog back into human form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.800
while the twelve remaining specimens had yet to be&nbsp;
presented with a magical cure for their condition.&nbsp;

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:09.120
Or perhaps seeing something as simple as a&nbsp;
children’s book reminded some of the frogs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:13.760
of all they were still to do in their&nbsp;
old lives – like starting families – and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.040
now they wouldn’t get the chance.
Kate and some of the other frogs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:21.280
began writing notes to Thomson and another&nbsp;
of the researchers who had been feeding them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:24.560
Fillis. They did their best to be&nbsp;
reasonable with the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:27.840
but also communicate how desperately&nbsp;
they wanted to be set free.&nbsp;

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:33.120
“You have no right to keep us here.” Kate wrote,&nbsp;
under the towering stare of Fillis and Thomson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:36.560
feeling for the first time in a long while&nbsp;
that she was actively doing something to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:41.840
make a difference in nature. “We need to&nbsp;
be out in the world, we need to be free!”&nbsp;

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:46.720
If she had more space on the paper, she would’ve&nbsp;
tried to note down suggestions of places the frogs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:51.920
could be introduced where they wouldn’t pose any&nbsp;
risk of disrupting the local ecosystem. The swamps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:58.160
of Louisiana where the SCP-306 fungus had been&nbsp;
found were one such idea that came to mind. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:03.280
much to Doctor Kate Barker’s disappointment, she&nbsp;
and her fellow frogs would only cause the fungi’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:08.560
infectious properties to spread, meaning their&nbsp;
pleas with the Foundation fell on deaf ears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:14.160
There was no other choice, nothing else&nbsp;
they could do: they needed to break out.&nbsp;

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:18.240
As night fell, Kate organized the frogs,&nbsp;
gradually writing out instructions for how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:23.040
they were going to escape, communicating with&nbsp;
them the same way she had with the researchers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:28.400
Only this time, the others listened. Even if they&nbsp;
couldn’t be human again, they didn’t want to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:33.440
the rest of their short lifespans being locked up&nbsp;
and tested forever. Kate marked down the time that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:38.320
Thomson and Fillis usually fed the frogs, and&nbsp;
drew up a detailed strategy. If she could hide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:43.280
for long enough under the others, it might make&nbsp;
it seem like one of the specimens was missing…&nbsp;

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:50.080
The next day, Researcher Thomson and Researcher&nbsp;
Fillis arrived to feed the SCP-306-1 specimens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:54.160
accompanied by security guards as always.&nbsp;
While her colleague went to collect the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.160 --> 00:17:00.080
feed for her to administer, Fillis did a count&nbsp;
of the frogs. Eleven. She counted again, only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:05.040
to get the same result. There was one missing.&nbsp;
As she leaned closer to the tank, Kate trusted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:09.840
her fellow amphibians above to follow the plan.
In a flash, the mass of frogs had leaped from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:14.960
their confinement and pinned Fillis to the&nbsp;
ground as one. The room erupted into chaos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:19.760
people-turned-frogs leaping in all directions as&nbsp;
they scattered and made a mad dash for freedom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:23.600
A gunshot rang out from one of the security&nbsp;
guards trying to subdue the creatures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:27.520
only for the stray shot to catch Researcher&nbsp;
Thomson in the neck, killing him.&nbsp;

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:33.120
Leading the charge on her tiny, rubbery legs,&nbsp;
Kate jumped closer and closer to the exit. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:39.440
so close. If she could just get far enough away,&nbsp;
she might finally be free to get back to nature.&nbsp;

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:45.120
Now go and check out “SCP-323 THE WENDIGO SKULL”&nbsp;
to hear another terrifying tale of an anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:49.600
that could cause someone to undergo a horrific&nbsp;
transformation process. Or if you’re in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:56.480
mood for more particularly peculiar plant&nbsp;
life, why not try “SCP-2800 CACTUSMAN”!

